{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784591264,"nonce":"HyCbK3dv9WUc03C4MqcLQx68gU0=","title":"Symptom","message":"The Helm chart renders a first-class env var `SCARAB_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET`\nfrom a chart value, but has no equivalent first-class value for\n`SCARAB_FORGEJO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` — even though the Forgejo forge adapter ships\n(`crates/scarab-forge-forgejo`, endpoint `/webhooks/forgejo`). Operators\ndeploying Forgejo webhooks must fall back to a raw `envFrom`/existingSecret\nworkaround. Asymmetric chart coverage vs GitHub.\n\nEvidence\n- deploy/helm/scarab/templates/secret.yaml:24-26 renders\n  `SCARAB_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET` from `.Values.secrets.githubWebhookSecret`;\n  there is no `forgejoWebhookSecret` / `SCARAB_FORGEJO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` key.\n- deploy/helm/scarab/values.yaml:91-92 documents `githubWebhookSecret` and\n  explicitly tells operators to set `SCARAB_FORGEJO_WEBHOOK_SECRET` \"via\" the\n  envFrom workaround instead of a first-class value.\n- deploy/helm/scarab/README.md:58-59 names both env vars per endpoint, so the\n  Forgejo secret is a supported knob that the chart just doesn't surface.\n\nSuggested fix (low-effort)\nAdd a `secrets.forgejoWebhookSecret` value mirroring `githubWebhookSecret`:\n- secret.yaml: `{{- with .Values.secrets.forgejoWebhookSecret }}`\n  `SCARAB_FORGEJO_WEBHOOK_SECRET: {{ . | quote }}` `{{- end }}`\n- values.yaml: document the new key alongside `githubWebhookSecret`\n- README.md: note it renders from the chart value like the GitHub one\n\nADR refs: ADR-0045 / ADR-0046 (forge auth + multi-adapter, GitHub + Forgejo).","files":null}]}